a three-hour visit with  major geopolitical significance the  three u.s senators touching down in  taiwan  and promising to give the island 750 000  covert 19 vaccines a show of support and  gratitude to taiwan  for sending supplies to the u.s during  the peak of its own outbreak in 2020  we are here as friends because we know  that taiwan  is experiencing a challenging time right  now which is why it was especially  important for the three of us to be here  in a bipartisan way  friends come to each other's aid  taiwan was initially one of the  pandemics success stories  last year it went more than eight months  without any domestic  transmission but it's recently had a  surge of infections  recording most of its more than two  hundred and twenty deaths in the past  month  we are very thankful to the biden  administration for extending a helping  hand and putting taiwan in the first  group of countries to receive the  vaccines shared by the u.s  these vaccines are a lifesaver to taiwan  we will not forget your help  fewer than three percent of the island's  23 million people  have been vaccinated this week more than  one million doses were donated by japan  taiwan has signed contracts for doses  from astrazeneca and moderna  and it's accused china of interfering in  potential deals to secure vaccines from  pfizer  some though blame inefficiencies by the  taiwanese authorities  and china says taiwan's governing party  is preventing it from sending doses of  its own vaccines  chinese-made medical products are banned  under taiwanese law  the authorities have obstructed the  mainland from sending vaccines to taiwan  in every possible way and even falsely  claimed  that the mainland has hindered its  procurement of vaccines for their own  political interest  the authorities continue to engage in  political manipulation  china's governing communist party views  the island as a part of its territory  and has vowed to one day seize it by  force if necessary  their complex relationship has seen  taiwan effectively locked out of  membership  of the world health organization the  united states is donating vaccines to  multiple places around the world as  china is  and that's just part of the competition  between the united states and china  to maintain relationships worldwide and  that would include  taiwan washington remains taiwan's  biggest ally  senators promising the island that it  will not face the pandemic alone  alexi o'brien al jazeera
 

